    what: 'Application security is the discipline of designing, building and operating software that resists attack: protecting confidentiality (data not leaked), integrity (data not tampered with) and availability (service not denied). For web developers it centers on the OWASP Top 10 — injection, broken auth, XSS, access control failures — and the browser/protocol mechanisms (TLS, same-origin policy, cookies, tokens) that defenses are built on.',
    why: 'Every input field, header, cookie and dependency is attack surface. Product companies ask security questions because a single XSS or IDOR ships customer data to attackers, and because engineers who understand attacks write defenses by default instead of bolting them on after the pentest report.',
