      answer: 'Assess: is the vulnerable code path actually reachable in your usage, and how severe/exploitable is it? Map the tree (npm ls / lockfile) to find what pulls it in. Remediate: bump to a patched version, or use overrides/resolutions to force the fixed transitive version, or mitigate temporarily (disable the feature, add a WAF rule) if no patch exists. Verify with audit/scan, deploy, confirm. Then prevent recurrence: scanning in CI, lockfile discipline, smaller dependency surface.',
      deepDive: 'Reachability analysis avoids panic-patching unreachable code; have a rollback/test plan since forced transitive bumps can break compatibility. For the broader supply-chain threat (malicious versions, not just CVEs): pin versions, review changelogs before upgrading, use SRI for CDN scripts, and consider an internal registry/allow-list. event-stream is the cautionary tale for blind auto-update.',
